{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 recorded below-seam ambient config/credential reads in the reconciler JIRA adapter/credential surface as `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`. RP-04 is not complete while these sit below the seams enforced by the in-process AST gate `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent C3a: 6633-219e-988a-42f6; grandparent C3: 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab. Disjoint file subtree from sibling C3a-CORE (ba8b).\n\nThe 12 flagged reads (path :: symbol), all drained:\n- `access_check.py` :: JIRA_URL, JIRA_USER, JIRA_PROJECT (probe scope + probe client)\n- `adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py` :: JIRA_URL, JIRA_USER, JIRA_PROJECT, load_config (2 sites: `_acli_call_timeout` L86, `resolve_jira_settings` L119)\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py` :: REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE, os.environ.get (`_rebar_env` shim body)\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py` :: load_config (2 sites: `resolve_comment_max_chars` L83, `resolve_jira_datacenter_settings` L97)\n- `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py` :: load_config (`cutover_clients` L90)\n- `adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py` :: load_config (`_pandoc_timeout` L352)\n\n(All under `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/`.) Affected SOURCE files: the 6 above, plus `src/rebar/config.py` (owned resolvers) and `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py` (removes the rows).\n\n## Why the JIRA_* reads are flagged (gate mechanism — from the gate code)\nThe gate's `_resolved_env` classifies `os.environ.get(\"X\")` as owner=**credential** IFF `X` is a derived credential name, else owner=**composition**. Derived names come live from `rebar._child_env._ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES` = ONLY the send secrets `JIRA_API_TOKEN` and `JIRA_PAT`; its comment states JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT are *intentionally absent* (non-secret). So JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT are owner=**composition** env-reads, and a credential-boundary file (access_check.py, acli_subprocess.py, jira_datacenter/settings.py) owns ONLY owner=credential reads, NOT composition ones. **So making them direct `os.environ.get(\"JIRA_URL\")` literals in the boundary would STILL be owner=composition → still flagged.** The correct cut routes them through an OWNED `config.py` resolver (basename config.py is a composition root that owns env-reads). The `JIRA_API_TOKEN`/`JIRA_PAT` reads here are owner=credential, already OWNED, out of scope.\n\n## Decision rule\n- **(a) CUT-TO-SEAM (default; 11 of 12 reads).** A read whose value is composed config is routed through an owned `config.py` resolver (reuse `compose_config()`/`load_config()`; add narrow named resolvers), so the ambient read moves into the composition root. Each adapter helper delegates to the owned resolver INTERNALLY (signature unchanged) — see cut details. **Preserve timing:** the JIRA endpoint + reconciler knobs resolve LIVE per operation today (env overrides file, re-read each call); the new resolvers read live per call — never composed once and threaded — so a mid-pass env override is not silently lost.\n- **(b) OWNED-IN-PLACE via `# read-via:` marker (bounded allowlist ONLY).** A read that is NOT composed config — a subsystem debug switch — stays with a `# read-via:` marker naming the category. Capped and enumerated below.\n\n### Owned-in-place allowlist (1 read = 1 marked line — the cap)\n1. `outbound_fields.py` `REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE` — subsystem debug switch (`=1` emits a one-line side-car RECON record per field-diff; off by default; not in the config schema). 1 marked line. No other listed read is marked.\n\n## Cut details (treatment a; each helper delegates internally, signatures unchanged)\n- **`access_check.py` JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT** (`_resolve_probe_scope`, `_build_probe_client`): read the non-secret trio from an injectable `env` mapping (default `os.environ`), live per probe. Add owned `config.py` `resolve_jira_endpoint(env=None) -> (url,user,project)` reading the env layer live (accepts an injected mapping for test parity). Both helpers delegate INTERNALLY; the `JIRA_API_TOKEN` read stays in-boundary (owned).\n- **`acli_subprocess.py`**: `resolve_jira_settings` (L119 load_config + L127-129 env fallback) → non-secret url/user/project resolution (env-over-file precedence + `InsecureUrlError` fail-loud / `ConfigError` degrade) moves into an owned `config.py` resolver; the helper delegates and appends env-only `JIRA_API_TOKEN` (owned). `_acli_call_timeout` (L86) → owned `config.py` `resolve_acli_timeout()` (same 0/negative→default clamp).\n- **`jira_datacenter/settings.py`**: `resolve_comment_max_chars` (L83) and `resolve_jira_datacenter_settings` (L97) delegate to owned `config.py` resolvers preserving FAIL-LOUD (no `except ConfigError`) and `>0 else 0=unlimited`; `JIRA_PAT` stays in-boundary.\n- **`jira_family/rich_text.py`** `cutover_clients` (L90) and **`wiki_render.py`** `_pandoc_timeout` (L352) delegate to owned `config.py` resolvers (same `ConfigError`→default fallback).\n- **`outbound_fields.py` `os.environ.get`**: the module-local `_rebar_env` shim serves only the single VERBOSE read; inline that read to a literal `os.environ.get(\"REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE\", \"0\")` (marked, treatment b) and DELETE the unused shim — the dynamic read no longer exists (verified: one caller here; siblings have own copies).\n\nSerena `find_referencing_symbols` confirms no helper call site needs a signature change.\n## Affected TEST consumers (updated in-scope, run in regression)\nDrive the cut env/config through the new owned resolvers / typed config: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/{test_config_jira_wiring,test_config_file_wiring,test_acli_subprocess_timeout}.py`; `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/{test_jira_dc_config_settings,test_rich_text_cutover,test_wiki_render_hardening,test_dc_pat_required_heldout}.py`; probe tests `tests/scripts/bridge/test_jira_capability_probe.py`. Assertions preserved; only the injection seam changes.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\nHeld-out oracle `tests/scripts/test_reconciler_jira_seam_clean_heldout.py` (imports gate scripts by bare name: `import check_config_ownership`) asserts: (i) `check_config_ownership.check(REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding whose path is any of the 6 listed source files; (ii) `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` has zero entries whose `path` is a listed source file; (iii) `# read-via:` markers across the 6 listed files total exactly **1**, confined to `outbound_fields.py` — every other listed file has 0 — so blanket-marking cannot substitute for cutting. RED now.\nBehavior regressions kept green: JIRA endpoint env-over-file LIVE precedence (a mid-pass `JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT` override is still observed after the cut), `resolve_jira_settings` insecure-url fail-loud + malformed-config degrade, DC fail-loud, and the acli timeout clamp — via the consumers above plus `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler` contracts.\n\n## Portability\nThe gate is in-process AST with no CI-provider trigger; the cutover adds no CI dependency.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nNo stored-format or config-key changes; env/file precedence and defaults are byte-preserved. Cut-to-seam is routing/delegation; the 1 marked line is inline. Rollback = revert the change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The 11 composed-config reads are cut-to-seam through owned `config.py` resolvers, live-per-call for the JIRA endpoint + reconciler knobs; no ambient config read remains below the seam in the 6 listed files.\n- [ ] Exactly 1 read (`REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE`) is owned-in-place with a `# read-via:` marker; no other listed read is marked.\n- [ ] The secret `JIRA_API_TOKEN`/`JIRA_PAT` boundary reads are unchanged (owner=credential, owned).\n- [ ] The 12 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows are removed; `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out oracle incl. its marker-total==1 / per-file-placement check).\n- [ ] The Testing regressions pass: JIRA-endpoint live-precedence, insecure-url fail-loud, DC fail-loud, and acli-timeout-clamp each verified; deltas noted as a comment on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787108178811401001,"uuid":"e41f878f-043b-46ca-bc1e-3796bb213184"}